  "worked_solution": "First, we calculate the velocity vector $v.$ Differentiating the position vector, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v & =\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}t} \\\\  & =\u27e8\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t},\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\u27e9 \\\\  & =\u27e8\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{2}\\operatorname{ln}\u2061t),\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(2{t}^{2}+9)\u27e9 \\\\  & =\u27e82t\\operatorname{ln}\u2061t+t,4t\u27e9.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo find the velocity when $t=e,$ we substitute in the above:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v(e) & =\u27e82e\\operatorname{ln}\u2061e+e,4e\u27e9 \\\\  & =\u27e83e,4e\u27e9\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo find the speed at $t=e$ we calculate the magnitude of $v(e),$ and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|v(e)| & =\\sqrt{(3e)^{2}+(4e)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{25{e}^{2}} \\\\  & =5e.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
